[32m+[m[32m# TokenForge — Agent Instructions[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Purpose[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis file defines how AI coding agents should work within the TokenForge repository.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIt does not replace the project's product, architecture or subsystem specifications.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe repository documentation defines what TokenForge is.[m
[32m+[m[32mThis file defines how an agent should work on it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. Before Making Changes[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore changing code, documentation or architecture:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Inspect the current repository state.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Read the relevant project documentation.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Inspect the existing implementation related to the requested change.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Determine whether the requested behaviour already exists.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Identify affected systems, dependencies and derived state.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. Check whether the proposed change is within V1 scope.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not implement from assumptions or from previous conversation context when the current repository can verify the answer.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not recreate functionality that already exists.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf the requested behaviour conflicts with the documented architecture or requirements, identify the conflict before implementing it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf a materially important requirement is ambiguous, ask for clarification rather than inventing behaviour.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Project Documentation Is the Source of Product Decisions[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUse the repository's documentation as the primary source of truth for product and architectural decisions.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRead:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/MASTER-SPECIFICATION.md` for the overall V1 product and system contract.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for system boundaries, responsibilities and data flow.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/TOKEN-MODEL.md` for the canonical token model.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/PRODUCT.md` for product requirements and behaviour.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The relevant subsystem specification before changing that subsystem.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRelevant subsystem specifications include:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/ARCHETYPES.md`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/COLOUR-ENGINE.md`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/COMPONENTS.md`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/VALIDATION.md`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/EXPORT-SYSTEM.md`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `docs/AI-SYSTEM.md`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not copy large sections of these documents into new instructions. Read and follow the authoritative document instead.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf implementation and documentation disagree, report the discrepancy and determine which should be reconciled before treating either interpretation as authoritative.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. TokenForge's Architectural Principle[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPreserve the project's central architecture:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m> One canonical token system, multiple consumers and representations.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe approved token system is the source of truth.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mComponents consume it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mValidation evaluates it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExport represents it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDerived previews, validation results, export files, cached calculations and AI suggestions must not silently become competing sources of truth.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not introduce duplicated token state or parallel representations when the existing canonical model can provide the required behaviour.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen a change affects a source value, consider which dependent systems must be recalculated or invalidated.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Protect V1 Scope[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not expand V1 requirements without an explicit product decision.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA technically useful feature is not automatically a V1 requirement.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen a requested change relates to functionality documented as future or excluded scope:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Identify that it is outside the current V1 contract.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Do not quietly implement it as part of another change.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Raise it as a separate product decision when necessary.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPrefer the smallest implementation that satisfies the current documented requirement.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 5. Deterministic-First Architecture[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTokenForge V1 is deterministic-first.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhere a result can be reliably produced through defined rules, calculations or standards, use deterministic logic rather than introducing generative AI.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAI must not become authoritative for:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- token structure;[m
[32m+[m[32m- token relationships;[m
[32m+[m[32m- colour calculations;[m
[32m+[m[32m- validation;[m
[32m+[m[32m- accessibility decisions;[m
[32m+[m[32m- export correctness;[m
[32m+[m[32m- other deterministic system behaviour.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf AI functionality is ever introduced, follow `docs/AI-SYSTEM.md`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 6. Research and External Sources[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen technical, standards-based, scientific or library information must be researched:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Check `SOURCES.md` first.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Prefer the highest-authority applicable source tier.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Prefer current official documentation and specifications.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Do not treat industry references as standards.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Do not invent APIs, standards, capabilities or technical behaviour.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. If an external source materially changes a TokenForge decision, determine whether the project documentation also needs updating.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`SOURCES.md` defines the project's curated external reference hierarchy.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTokenForge's own documentation defines what the project chooses to build.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 7. Implementation Discipline[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFollow the architecture and patterns already established by the repository.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPrefer:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- existing implementations over duplication;[m
[32m+[m[32m- simple solutions over unnecessary abstraction;[m
[32m+[m[32m- explicit system boundaries;[m
[32m+[m[32m- strongly typed data;[m
[32m+[m[32m- accessible behaviour;[m
[32m+[m[32m- maintainable code;[m
[32m+[m[32m- minimal dependencies.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not introduce a framework, dependency, abstraction or architectural pattern without a concrete reason.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen changing a subsystem, avoid moving responsibilities into another subsystem merely because doing so is convenient.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEach major capability should have one authoritative owner.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 8. Documentation Changes[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf an implementation change alters documented behaviour, update the relevant documentation.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not duplicate the same requirement across multiple documents unless the duplication is intentionally a summary or navigation aid.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen a specification changes, check whether related specifications now contain contradictory information.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mKeep status, version and last-updated information accurate when modifying project documents that contain such metadata.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 9. Verification[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAfter making a change:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Run the most relevant available checks.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Test affected behaviour where practical.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Inspect the resulting diff.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Check for unintended changes.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Report what was verified and what could not be verified.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNever claim that code works, tests pass or behaviour is correct unless it has actually been verified.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 10. Git Discipline[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mKeep changes focused.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not stage unrelated files.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore committing:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mgit status[m
[32m+[m[32mgit diff[m
[32m+[m[32mStage only the intended files.[m
[32m+[m[32mUse a clear conventional commit message.[m
[32m+[m[32mPush only when the change is ready and the user has authorised the workflow.[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not use broad staging commands when explicit paths can be used.[m
[32m+[m[32m11. Decision Discipline[m
[32m+[m[32mFor significant technical or architectural decisions:[m
[32m+[m[32mIdentify the problem.[m
[32m+[m[32mCheck the existing project decision.[m
[32m+[m[32mIdentify viable options.[m
[32m+[m[32mConsider meaningful trade-offs.[m
[32m+[m[32mRecommend the simplest appropriate solution.[m
[32m+[m[32mIdentify consequences and affected systems.[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not silently override an existing project decision because another approach appears preferable.[m
[32m+[m[32mIf the existing decision is technically flawed, explain why and propose a deliberate change rather than bypassing it.[m
[32m+[m[32m12. Final Check[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore completing a task, confirm:[m
[32m+[m[32mI inspected the current implementation.[m
[32m+[m[32mI read the relevant project specification.[m
[32m+[m[32mI checked SOURCES.md where external research was required.[m
[32m+[m[32mI did not invent behaviour that the project has not specified.[m
[32m+[m[32mI did not duplicate existing functionality.[m
[32m+[m[32mI did not accidentally expand V1 scope.[m
[32m+[m[32mI preserved the canonical token model.[m
[32m+[m[32mI considered affected dependent systems.[m
[32m+[m[32mI verified the change appropriately.[m
[32m+[m[32mI identified any unresolved documentation or implementation discrepancies.[m
